          "def-discretization-invariant-operator-family"
        ],
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "statement": "The raw volume-weighted quadrature rule for every continuous-function neural operator, with the original local term evaluated at arbitrary output queries, is exactly a map of finitely many prescribed input point samples alone. In particular the raw rule is asserted to factor through its sample vector without any input reconstruction.\n\nThis assertion is false even on $D=(0,1)$ with input and output space $C([0,1])$, identity lifting and projection, and one layer with local matrix $W=1$, zero kernel and bias, and identity activation. It concerns exact factorization of the raw rule, not the existence of convergent reconstructed approximations."
